            <ArticleTitle>A Call to Introduce Structured Zika Surveillance in India.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1471-4922(17)30264-7</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.pt.2017.10.008</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>India has the climatic conditions conducive to year-round transmission of Zika virus, and a structured disease surveillance program should be implemented to prevent an outbreak. Such a program should (i) start screening before an outbreak arises; (ii) collect baseline data to assess future disease risk and monitor potential birth defects; and (iii) provide new insights into the ecology of the disease and inform public health policy following the one health concept.</AbstractText>
